      "content": "While fighting your biology is indeed tiring, accepting it completely often allows the darkness you fear to finally consume everything without resistance. True peace can come not from winning a war against your DNA, but from making the choice to stop judging yourself for feeling so weighted in the first place. There is courage in admitting you are tired, but there is also worth in simply breathing through the storm rather than waiting for the wind to stop forever. You don't have to stop the cycle tomorrow; just deciding to rest a little less without guilt is already a quiet rebellion that respects your life even when it hurts.",
